      en: ["Spokane was founded in 1873 by James N. Glover.", "The Great Fire of 1889 destroyed over 32 square blocks of downtown Spokane.", "Expo '74 was the first environmentally themed World's Fair and drew about 5.6 million visitors.", "Riverfront Park, created for Expo '74, covers 100 acres (40 hectares).", "Spokane is known as the 'Lilac City' and hosts an annual Lilac Festival.", "Gonzaga University, a private Catholic university, was founded in Spokane in 1887."],
      es: ["Spokane tiene 229.207 habitantes (2023).", "La superficie de la ciudad es de 180 km².", "Fundada en 1871 como ciudad ferroviaria.", "El Riverfront Park se creó para la Expo '74.", "Las cascadas Spokane Falls tienen una caída de 12 m.", "El Aeropuerto Internacional de Spokane atiende a 2 millones de pasajeros."],
      pt: ["Spokane tem 229.207 habitantes (2023).", "A área da cidade é de 180 km².", "Fundada em 1871 como uma cidade ferroviária.", "O Riverfront Park foi criado para a Expo '74.", "As Spokane Falls têm uma queda de 12 m.", "O Aeroporto Internacional de Spokane serve 2 milhões de passageiros."],
      fr: ["Spokane compte 229 207 habitants (2023).", "La superficie de la ville est de 180 km².", "Fondée en 1871 en tant que ville ferroviaire.", "Le Riverfront Park a été créé pour l'Expo '74.", "Les Spokane Falls ont une hauteur de chute de 12 m.", "L'aéroport international de Spokane accueille 2 millions de passagers."],
